"required":["salesFunnelCampaign"]}}],"needsTheirYes":{"why":"Sets the whole sales funnel campaign running: it finds and contacts people and spends up to the funnel's max budget.","because":["starts_work","spends_money"],"notNeededWhen":[{"status":"stop"}],"neededWhen":[{"status":"activate"}]}}

describe_operation {"operationId":"postV1OrgsAudiencesSplit"} → {"operationId":"postV1OrgsAudiencesSplit","method":"POST","path":"/v1/orgs/audiences/split","summary":"Propose a split of a target audience into segments","description":"Proxy to human-service POST /orgs/audiences/split. Turns a target sentence into up to a few non-overlapping segments; persists nothing. One LLM call plus a typed judgment, so it can take up to a minute. Request + response shapes are owned by human-service. Downstream status and body (400 validation, 502 on an LLM error) are forwarded verbatim.

Request body: documented from human-service POST /orgs/audiences/split, which owns and validates it; the gateway forwards it unchanged.

Response: documented from human-service POST /orgs/audiences/split, which owns it; the gateway forwards it unchanged. Its full document: GET /v1/platform/services/human.","params":[],"body":{"type":"object","properties":{"brandId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"targetAudience":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The confirmed free-text answer to 'who do you sell to?' (e.g. 'B2B SaaS founders in the US and Europe')."}},"required":["brandId","targetAudience"]},"answers":[{"status":"200","description":"Proposed segments (human-service shape)","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"axes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["geography","company_size","industry","seniority_role"]},"description":"The axes the segments partition the target along: empty when a single segment is returned, one axis, or two axes crossed. Only axes a people search can filter on."},"segments":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"Short label, max 4 words, unique within the proposal."},"description":{"type":"string","description":"One plain-language sentence that fully specifies the segment on its own (who, where, what kind of company, plus this segment's partition value). Becomes the audience's description on confirm."},"icon":{"type":"string","enum":["globe-hemisphere-west","globe-hemisphere-east","map-pin","user","users-three","buildings","building-office","crown","briefcase","user-circle","rocket-launch","code","cpu","storefront","shopping-cart","factory","stethoscope","first-aid-kit","bank","scales","graduation-cap","megaphone","handshake","house-line","truck","fork-knife","airplane-tilt","leaf","paint-brush","heartbeat","target"],"description":"Phosphor icon name (kebab-case) from a closed vocabulary; `globe-hemisphere-west` renders as <GlobeHemisphereWest /> in @phosphor-icons/react."},"iconConfidence":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1,"description":"The judge's own certainty about the icon (decorative: the icon is always set)."}},"required":["name","description","icon","iconConfidence"]},"minItems":1,"maxItems":6,"description":"1 to 6 mutually exclusive segments that together cover the target. Nothing is persisted."}},"required":["axes","segments"]}}],"needsTheirYes":false}

describe_operation {"operationId":"postV1OrgsAudiences"} → {"operationId":"postV1OrgsAudiences","method":"POST","path":"/v1/orgs/audiences","summary":"Create an audience","description":"Proxy to human-service POST /orgs/audiences. Request + response shapes owned by human-service. Forwarded untransformed.

Request body: documented from human-service POST /orgs/audiences, which owns and validates it; the gateway forwards it unchanged.

Response: documented from human-service POST /orgs/audiences, which owns it; the gateway forwards it unchanged. Its full document: GET /v1/platform/services/human.","params":[],"body":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"brandId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"provider":{"type":"string","enum":["apollo","apify","crm","google_maps"],"description":"The provider this audience commits to. apollo/apify when persisting a candidate from /suggest; crm for a brand whose audience is its uploaded contact list (served by crm-service — no filters/apolloAudienceId, brand-scoped); google_maps for local businesses found on Google Maps (GMAPS-SOURCE-1103): state `nlPrompt` in plain words ("restaurants and cafes in Astana") and the Google Maps searches are written for you (needs x-user-id), or pass `filters: {google_maps: {queries, country, language}}` yourself. Each serve hands out one business: phone (E.164), website, address, no email, no person name. Omit for a neutral audience."},"nlPrompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"filters":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"nullable":true}},"apolloAudienceId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Pointer to the faithful Apollo audience owned by apollo-service, when persisting an apollo candidate. Omit for a neutral / apify audience."},"crmUploadId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"Bind this audience to ONE imported CRM source (a crm-service upload id of the same brand). Every CRM serve made under this audience is then restricted to the people of that file, so several bound audiences can coexist for one brand and each is independently pausable + independently costed. Validated against the brand's uploads at creation (400 if it is not one of them). Omit to keep the whole-brand behaviour. Immutable afterwards."},"crmPeople":{"type":"object","properties":{"signedUp":{"type":"boolean","description":"true = only people who signed up to the brand's product (a signup on its auth provider); false = only people who did not."},"replied":{"type":"boolean","description":"false = only people who NEVER wrote to the brand on any conversation channel (email, WhatsApp, LinkedIn, an answer to our outreach); true = only people who did."},"reachableBy":{"type":"string","enum":["phone","email"],"description":"Only people holding a phone / an email. A phone channel (WhatsApp, SMS) wants 'phone': a person served without one is burned for nothing."},"segment":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"nullable":true},"description":"A part of the brand's own CRM, as crm-service's PeopleSegment states it (passed through verbatim, validated by crm-service): dealStages [{stage, pipeline?}], dealStatuses, tags, reached / notReached (funnel steps), includeClients, includeOptedOut. Lists OR, keys AND; clients and opted-out people are out unless stated. Names come from crm-service GET /orgs/contacts/segments.","example":{"dealStages":[{"pipeline":"Sales Pipeline","stage":"Form Filled - No Appointment"}]}}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Bind this CRM audience to the brand's merged PEOPLE matching a filter (e.g. {signedUp: true, replied: false} = product signups who never answered) instead of to an imported file, optionally scoped to a `segment` of the brand's own CRM (e.g. {segment: {dealStages: [{pipeline: 'Sales Pipeline', stage: 'Form Filled - No Appointment'}]}}). Requires provider 'crm'; exclusive with crmUploadId. A segment crm-service refuses is a 400 carrying its reason. Every serve passes the filter to crm-service (same brand-wide no-re-serve forever); each served person carries its phone when crm-service holds one. Validated against crm-service's serve-stats at creation (its counts become the audience's Size / Remaining). Immutable afterwards."},"offerId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"The offer this audience belongs to — a brand-service offer id. Scopes the audience to one distinct thing the brand sells; name uniqueness becomes per (org, brand, offer), so two offers of the same brand may each own an audience with the same name. Stored as-is: human-service defines no offer semantics and does not resolve the id (same as brandId). Omit to keep the brand-wide behaviour. Immutable afterwards."},"apolloCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true,"minimum":0,"description":"Optional count snapshot the caller already obtained from /orgs/people/search/dry-run (apollo). Stored as-is; refresh-count re-computes it server-side later. Accepts null (e.g. an apify-source candidate carries apolloCount: null)."},"apifyCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true,"minimum":0,"description":"Optional apify count snapshot (see apolloCount). Accepts null (e.g. an apollo-source candidate carries apifyCount: null)."}},"required":["name","brandId"]},"answers":[{"status":"200","description":"Created audience","schema":{"truncated":true,"firstChars":"{"type":"object","properties":{"audience":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"orgId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"brandId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"name":{"type":"string"},"nlPrompt":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"description":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"One-sentence summary of who THIS audience targets, distinct from the shared batch nlPrompt. LLM-generated at /suggest time. null for rows predating this field."},"provider":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"enum":["apollo","apify","crm",null]},"apolloAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"Pointer to the faithful Apollo audience owned by apollo-service ('one filter vocabulary' Wave 2). Set for apollo audiences; null for apify (legacy) rows and pre-Wave-2 rows not yet backfilled. The faithful filters live in apollo-service; the `filters` field below is human-service's opaque cache of them."},"crmUploadId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"The ONE imported CRM source (crm-service upload id) this audience is bound to. When set, every CRM serve made under this audience is restricted to the people that came from that file, so several CRM audiences can coexist for one brand and each behaves as its own audience. null = unbound ⟹ the serve covers the brand's whole imported list (the pre-existing behaviour)."},"crmPeople":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"properties":{"signedUp":{"type":"boolean"},"replied":{"type":"boolean"},"reachableBy":{"type":"string","enum":["phone","email"]},"segment":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"nullable":true},"description":"A part of the brand's own CRM, as crm-service's PeopleSegment states it (passed through verbatim, validated by crm-service): dealStages [{stage, pipeline?}], dealStatuses, tags, reached / notReached (funnel steps), includeClients, includeOptedOut. Lists OR, keys AND; clients and opted-out people are out unless stated. Names come from crm-service GET /orgs/contacts/segments.","example":{"dealStages":[{"pipeline":"Sales Pipeline","stage":"Form Filled - No Appointment"}]}}},"description":"The PEOPLE-pool filter this CRM audience is bound to: every serve draws from the brand's merged people (everyone its connected tools know, one row per human) who match it, instead of from imported files. null = not people-bound (file-bound via crmUploadId, or the whole imported list)."},"crmPeopleByStage":{"type":"array","nullable":true,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"pipeline":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"stage":{"type":"string"},"served":{"type":"integer"},"remainingSendable":{"type":"integer"},"totalSendable":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["pipeline","stage","served","remainingSendable","totalSendable"]},"description":"A people-bound CRM audience whose segment names dealStages: crm-service's counts per stated stage (same snapshot as Size / Remaining). Entries overlap when a person holds deals at two of them. null otherwise."},"offerId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"The offer (Org > Brand > Offer